## Analyzing Survey Data

Survey analysis has three phases: collect raw responses, tally frequencies, and compute summary statistics.

### Phase 1: Collecting Responses

```xiom
fn main() -> Int {
  let responses: Vec[Int] = Vec[Int].new();
  responses.push(5); responses.push(4); responses.push(5);
  responses.push(3); responses.push(5); responses.push(2);
  responses.push(4); responses.push(5); responses.push(1);
  responses.push(5);
  return 0;
}
```

### Phase 2: Frequency Tally

```xiom
fn tally_ratings(responses: &Vec[Int]) -> Map[Int, Int] {
  let tally: Map[Int, Int] = Map[Int, Int].new();
  let i = 0;
  while i < responses.len() {
    let r = match responses.get(i) { Some(v) => v, None => 0 };
    let count = match tally.get(&r) { Some(c) => c, None => 0 };
    tally.insert(r, count + 1);
    i = i + 1;
  }
  return tally;
}
```

### Phase 3: Summary Statistics

```xiom
fn compute_average(responses: &Vec[Int]) -> Float64 {
  let total = 0;
  let i = 0;
  while i < responses.len() {
    let r = match responses.get(i) { Some(v) => v, None => 0 };
    total = total + r;
    i = i + 1;
  }
  return int_to_float(total) / int_to_float(responses.len());
}

fn count_perfect_scores(tally: &Map[Int, Int]) -> Int {
  return match tally.get(&5) { Some(c) => c, None => 0 };
}

fn find_consensus(tally: &Map[Int, Int], ratings: &Vec[Int]) -> Int {
  let best_rating = 0;
  let max_count = 0;
  let i = 0;
  while i < ratings.len() {
    let r = match ratings.get(i) { Some(v) => v, None => 0 };
    let count = match tally.get(&r) { Some(c) => c, None => 0 };
    if count > max_count {
      max_count = count;
      best_rating = r;
    }
    i = i + 1;
  }
  return best_rating;
}
```

### The Full Report

```xiom
fn main() -> Int {
  let responses: Vec[Int] = Vec[Int].new();
  responses.push(5); responses.push(4); responses.push(5);
  responses.push(3); responses.push(5); responses.push(2);
  responses.push(4); responses.push(5); responses.push(1);
  responses.push(5);

  let tally = tally_ratings(&responses);
  io.println("Total responses: " + string.int_to_str(responses.len()));
  io.println("Perfect 5s: " + string.int_to_str(count_perfect_scores(&tally)));
  io.println("Most common: " + string.int_to_str(find_consensus(&tally, &responses)));
  return 0;
}
```

Three data structures working together: Vec for raw data, Map for counting, and summary functions for the story behind the numbers.

